<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8" standalone="yes"?>
<!--
  <summary>
  The pieces of Home that a settings preview stage draws as well as Home
  itself (STAGE-GROUNDWORK, roadmap item 47, 05/11/2026): the stats column,
  the logo, the weather line, the clock, the version footer and the
  Continue Watching and Recently Added tabs. Home.xml includes them in the
  order it always drew them.
  </summary>
  <remarks>
  Every toggle a piece reads takes a flip parameter, false by default, and
  the read is written as an exclusive or with it: with the parameter false
  the piece follows the setting exactly as before, with it true the piece
  shows the setting the other way round, which is how a stage shows what OK
  would do while a row is focused, without writing anything. Home never
  passes a flip, so nothing on Home changes.

  What the pieces assume of Home, for the stage that will draw them in
  Skin Settings (sub item 2): the Home window's properties hold whatever
  window draws them, but the tab expressions continue_tab_shown and
  recent_tab_shown count Home's own containers (9201, 9203, 9221, 9223)
  and read 0 elsewhere; the weather button and the tabs carry Home ids
  (9006, 9210 to 9213) and navigate to Home ids (9000, 9100 to 9120), and
  9000 and 9006 are also ids in SkinSettings.xml. So the stage passes its
  own shown conditions for the tabs and draws no button of these pieces
  with a live id. Nothing draws them outside Home until then.
  </remarks>
-->
<includes>
	<!-- <summary>STAGE-GROUNDWORK, 05/11/2026: the stats column, moved out of Home.xml unchanged. flip_movies and flip_tvshows show a block the other way round while true; Home leaves them false.</summary> -->
